    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nCreating multicursor in Visual mode replays keys that are not supposed to be replayed.\n\nThe bisected culprit is 493a4dd57127de50c76e6a627bff27c64d5adf91.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean -- Makefile`\n2. `:xnoremap <expr> is \"ip\"`\n3. Type `j` - `vis` - `Q`. It adds `sQ` at the start of each paragraph line except the top one.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`Q` in Visual mode adds extra cursor on each line always without replaying unnecessary keys.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1600+g4cad27fbcf\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.2.3-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
